{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2187-02-06 15:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the vascular surgery team. I understand you've been having some swelling in your neck and arms again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2187-02-06 15:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been getting worse over the last few days. It’s like the last time—swelling, headaches, blurry vision, especially when I lie back or lift my arms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2187-02-06 15:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds consistent with your SVC syndrome. We’re concerned the vein might be narrowing again. We’ll start with some imaging to check the blood flow in your neck veins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2187-02-06 15:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time they did an ultrasound. Is that what you’re planning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2187-02-06 15:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve ordered a limited neck ultrasound to look at your internal jugular veins. That’ll help us see if they’re open and flowing properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—the ultrasound shows both your internal jugular veins are patent and compressible. No clots there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why am I still so swollen then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The blockage might be further down, in the superior vena cava itself. We’re planning a venogram tomorrow to get a detailed look at that area."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they try to open it during the test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if we see a narrowing, we’ll attempt a venoplasty or stent placement. But we’ll know more once we see the images."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m just worried it won’t work again, like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. We’ll do our best. In the meantime, we’re also checking on your Crohn’s symptoms—you mentioned nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been nauseous. I think my Crohn’s is flaring again. My stomach’s been tender."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2187-02-07 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "GI has been consulted. They’ll evaluate you and make sure we’re not missing an obstruction or ileus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2187-02-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to take you down for the venogram. It’s a procedure where we inject dye into your veins and take X-rays to see the blood flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2187-02-08 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember this from before. Is it safe with my allergies?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2187-02-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your allergies, especially to iodine-based contrast. We’ll use a low-risk agent and monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2187-02-08 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well during the procedure. We found significant obstruction in your SVC, but unfortunately, the stent placement wasn’t successful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2187-02-08 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. What happens now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2187-02-08 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve consulted cardiothoracic surgery. You may need an open surgical bypass. They’ll set up a future date for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2187-02-08 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds serious. Is it safe after all my other surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2187-02-08 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s complex, but they’ll evaluate your full history. For now, we’ll manage your symptoms and plan the next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2187-02-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also got your blood culture results back. One came back with coagulase-negative staph and Enterococcus faecium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2187-02-08 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that an infection? I’ve had line infections before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2187-02-08 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We started you on IV antibiotics just in case, but you’ve been afebrile and your white count is normal. It’s likely a contaminant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2187-02-08 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So you’re stopping the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2187-02-08 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discontinuing them. No need to treat if it’s not a real infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2187-02-08 22:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray to check your Crohn’s symptoms. The first one was hard to read, but today’s shows distended colon loops."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2187-02-08 22:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it a blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2187-02-08 22:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks like ileus—slowed bowel movement—common with Crohn’s flares. No surgical obstruction seen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2187-02-08 22:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need more treatment for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2187-02-08 22:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "GI cleared you. We’ll manage nausea with medication and let your bowel rest. Most improve with time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2187-02-09 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat blood cultures showed no growth. Confirms the earlier result was likely contamination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2187-02-09 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about another infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2187-02-09 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We were too, but you’re stable. Your neck swelling is still there, but not worsening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2187-02-09 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my Crohn’s symptoms are a little better. Less nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2187-02-09 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll keep supporting you until discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Already? What about the SVC blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The venogram confirmed the obstruction, but we couldn’t fix it. Surgery is the next step—we’ll schedule that as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my medications? I was on a lot before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve simplified them. You’ll continue levothyroxine, citalopram, and pain meds as needed. We added Cipro in case your Crohn’s flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the contrast dye from the test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Drink plenty of fluids—about 2 liters today—to help flush it out. Avoid metformin for two days, just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the bandage at the procedure site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Remove the pressure bandage tonight, use a clean band-aid. Keep it dry—no showering for now. Watch for bruising or lumps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go up and down stairs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Limit stair climbing today. No lifting over 10 pounds for three days. Rest as much as possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see cardiothoracic surgery to plan the bypass. GI follow-up in a few weeks. Call us if swelling worsens or you develop fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel better knowing what’s next."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2187-02-10 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get the discharge papers ready. Take care, and we’ll see you soon in clinic."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2187-02-06 15:48:00",
    "admission_end": "2187-02-10 16:26:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a history of Crohn’s disease, short bowel syndrome, and SVC syndrome was admitted with worsening symptoms of superior vena cava obstruction, including neck swelling, headache, blurry vision, and nausea. Imaging confirmed patent internal jugular veins, but a diagnostic SVC-IVC venogram revealed persistent SVC obstruction. An attempted stent placement was unsuccessful, and cardiothoracic surgery was consulted for future bypass planning. A blood culture showed coagulase-negative staph and Enterococcus faecium, but antibiotics were discontinued as the result was deemed a contaminant. Abdominal imaging indicated ileus related to a Crohn’s flare, managed conservatively. The patient improved symptomatically and was discharged home with a plan for outpatient surgical evaluation, medication adjustments, and follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Compression of vein",
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption",
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism"
    ]
  }
}
